 "Esection": {
  "value": "\\subsection{Exploratory: what helps instead}\nA Kansal-style predictive duty cycle~\\cite{kansal2007} did beat blackout on TEST (median -0.015). We registered three follow-up predictions before running a dedicated post-test stage; all three failed, so the result is reported as an observation only (Figs.~\\ref{fig:q2} and~\\ref{fig:q2b}). The controller spends spilled energy (median mean activation 1.64 times that of blackout), but at equal mean activation it is indistinguishable from periodic operation (median difference -0.0008, with the predicted sign in only 56.6\\,\\% of cases and the opposite sign significant in 5 of 25 cells). Its gain is also far smaller than the difference of the two floors (median -0.098 predicted, $R^2=-4.5$ around the identity line), because it concentrates activations in daytime and still has outages, so it pays the Jensen gap of Corollary~\\ref{cor:jensen} and the outage term of Proposition~\\ref{prop:blackout}. A constant rate sized on the TRAIN months to never black out did worse than both (median +0.11 against blackout, better than both in 3.7\\,\\% of 3{,}007 cases). Theorem~\\ref{thm:energy} bounds schedules that never empty storage; on these traces, accepting short outages and spending the surplus is the better operating point.\n\\begin{figure}[!t]\\centering\\includegraphics[width=\\columnwidth]{figures/F6p_throttle_kansal_amax_test.pdf}\\caption{Miss relative to blackout against capacity (medians over the TEST cases in which periodic $K=8$ has outages). Exploratory (post-test) analysis.}\\label{fig:q2}\\end{figure}\n\\begin{figure}[!t]\\centering\\includegraphics[width=\\columnwidth]{figures/F7_kansal_obs_vs_pred_test.pdf}\\caption{Observed Kansal--blackout miss difference against the difference of the two floors (Theorem~\\ref{thm:floor}); points above the dashed line gain less than the floors suggest. Exploratory (post-test) analysis.}\\label{fig:q2b}\\end{figure}",
  "source": "exploratory_q2_test.json / exploratory_q2_boot_test.json",
  "note": ""
 },
 "EabstractSentence": {
  "value": "a predictive controller that spends spilled energy misses fewer events (median -0.015), a post-test observation whose registered explanations were not confirmed.",
  "source": "exploratory_q2_test.json / exploratory_q2_boot_test.json",
  "note": ""
